We add $\goldD{\dfrac{81}{4}}$ inside the parentheses, and subtract $\greenD{1}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{81}{4}}$ outside them, to keep the expression equivalent.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\greenD{} \left(x^2 -9 x\right) +14
\\\\
&=\greenD{}\left(x^2 -9 x+\goldD{\dfrac{81}{4}}\right) +14 -\greenD{1}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{81}{4}}
\\\\
&= \left(x -\dfrac{9}{2}\right)^2 +14 -\dfrac{81}{4}
\\\\
&= \left(x -\dfrac{9}{2}\right)^2 -\dfrac{25}{4}
\end{align}$
